//! The Rust exe patches (`docs/notes/rust_patches.md`): the arena's block
//! `patches.code`, one crate in three layers.
//!
//! - `raw`: generated by engine_026g.py from `engine_026g.tsv` and
//!   `fields_026g.tsv`: the game's functions (each called directly in its
//!   own convention, or through its cdecl thunk), kernel32's imports, the
//!   address of each field. Unsafe, no logic.
//! - [`vostok`]: the engine's safe API over `raw` (handles, enums,
//!   newtypes; the only `unsafe` blocks, each with its invariant), and the
//!   runtime: the hook context, the log, the panic handler.
//! - The patches, a module each ([`suicide_key`]): `#![forbid(unsafe_code)]`,
//!   `vostok` alone.
//!
//! `hooks` is generated by link_026g.py from patch_026g.py's `RUST_HOOKS`:
//! each hook's shim, from the registers at the game's site to the patch's
//! function. link_026g.py refuses an address, a `transmute` or an `extern`
//! block outside `raw`, and a patch module that names `raw` or allows
//! `unsafe`.

#![cfg_attr(not(test), no_std)]

mod raw {
    include!("../../../engine_026g.rs");
}
mod hooks {
    include!("../../../hooks_026g.rs");
}
pub mod vostok;

pub mod suicide_key;
